{
  "Band headers": "",
  "A band is a header that spans several columns. Give it a `title` and the `columns` under it, which can be columns or other bands to any depth. The header gains one row per band level above the column titles, with each band spanning its columns. A column can be dragged only within its band, and dragging a band moves its columns with it. A band is pinned, hidden and moved as a whole, from its own menu (its header button or Alt+Down) or with `columnOption` by its `name`. In this example, “Payment” spans three columns, and “Order” spans two columns and the “Delivery” band.": "",
  "Band field": "",
  "The band's caption and its contents: columns and bands, to any depth. A band holds no data.": "",
  "`band-` and its position": "",
  "Its identity in the layout, `columnOption`, `columnSettings` and the events (`band-1`, or `band-1-2` when nested, if none is given).": "",
  "Bands specified as a flat list: a band with `isBand`, and columns or bands that reference it in `ownerBand`, by `name` or by its position in `columns`.": "",
  "The `bandAlign` setting": "",
  "The position of the caption above its columns.": "",
  "Pins or hides the band with all its columns. A column inside a band uses its band's side, and pinning it pins the band.": "",
  "The grid's settings": "",
  "What the user can do with the band: drag it among its neighbors, hide it, pin it and open its menu.": "",
  "Custom content in the band's header, created once. Provides `ctx.band` and `ctx.title`.": "",
  "The position of captions when a band does not specify one.": "",
  "Band behavior": "",
  "A column moves only among the columns and bands of its own band, and a band among those beside it, both within their pinned zone and not across an item that cannot move (`movable: false`). They move by dragging the header, with “Move” in the menu and the arrow keys, or with `columnOption(name, 'visibleIndex', n)`.": "",
  "Columns resize as usual (drag the edge of a column's header, or double-click to fit), and a band follows its columns.": "",
  "A band's header does not sort and has no filter, but its columns work as usual.": "",
  "Hiding every column of a band hides the band, and hiding a band (from its menu or with `columnOption(name, 'visible', false)`) hides its columns. The last visible column stays.": "",
  "With bands, the column list is a tree with check boxes, with bands above their columns. A band's check box shows or hides all of them.": "",
  "`grid.layout` keeps the column order, widths and hidden state, plus `bands` with each band's hidden state and side. A band's position comes from its columns. A layout that splits a band reassembles it at its first column. `layoutKey` saves all of this.": "",
  "CSV writes one line per band level above the titles, with each band's title over its first column. `exportSheet()` adds header rows, and `merges` lists the cells a band (and a column spanning the band rows) covers, for the writer to merge.": "",
  "Only the header changes. The rows, the virtual list and paging work as usual.": "",
  "Band rows are `row` elements of `columnheader` cells in the header's row group. A band's header has the `aria-colindex` of its first column and an `aria-colspan` of its columns, the columns keep their own index, and band rows count in `aria-rowindex` and `aria-rowcount`. Above a pinned column with no band, an empty piece stays with the column so that the band rows scroll under it.": "",
  "Adaptive columns": "",
  "With `settings.columnHidingEnabled`, the grid hides columns while it is narrower than they are, starting from the last. With `hidingPriority` on some columns, only those hide, lowest first. A “…” column then opens a row's adaptive detail below it, showing the titles and values of the hidden columns (with editors where the row can be edited), one row at a time. This is calculated from the column widths and the grid's width (through a `ResizeObserver`), never from the rendered output, and recalculated whenever either changes. Drag the splitter to see it. Hidden columns still count as visible, so the column chooser, `getVisibleColumns()`, export and copying include them.": "",
  "Hides columns while the grid is narrower than they are, starting from the last, and shows them in the row's adaptive detail.": "",
  "When set on any column, only columns with a priority hide (even without `columnHidingEnabled`), lowest first. Pinned and grouped columns never hide.": "",
  "The form layout of the detail (the kit's `FormLayout`).": "",
  "Uses editors instead of text for cells the user can fill, in the `row`, `cell` and `batch` edit modes. They write into the row's draft, as its cells do.": "",
  "Editing a row with hidden columns it can fill opens its detail, and leaving the row closes it (the `row` edit mode).": "",
  "The width of the “…” column, and the keys on its cell that open and close the detail.": "",
  "The detail is a separate row directly after its row, before the row's master-detail when both are open. It is measured as it renders, is in the reading order (`aria-owns`), counts in `aria-rowindex`, and has one cell named “Hidden columns of row 3” (`gridAdaptiveOf`, with `gridAdaptive` naming the “…” and its column). Grouped rows, paging and the virtual list keep it below its row, and a wider grid with nothing hidden closes it.": "",
  "Moves to its band's header, and again to the band above.": "",
  "Moves to the first column or band under it.": "",
  "Moves along the bands of its row.": "",
  "Opens its menu: pin, move, hide the band, the column chooser and reset.": "",
  "Opens or closes the row's adaptive detail.": "",
  "Moves into the detail. From its last stop, it moves into the row's master-detail or, while the row is being edited, on to the next row's cells.": "",
  "Moves into the editors of its open adaptive detail.": "",
  "Returns to the row.": "",
  "Occurs before a row's detail lays out its form, when it opens and again when other columns hide or show. Change `formOptions` (`items`, which are the hidden fields or kit form items, plus `colCount`, `minColWidth` and `labelMode`).": "",
  "Occurs before a row's detail opens or closes, from its “…”, its keys or code. Set `cancel` to keep it as it is.": "",
  "Occurs after it opens or closes.": "",
  "Opens a row's detail by key (any open detail closes first), or closes the open one.": "",
  "Indicates whether that row's detail is open. Reactive.": "",
  "`string[]`, reactive": "",
  "The columns currently hidden by width, in display order.": "",
  "`grid.adaptiveDetail.colCount = 1`. `onOptionChanged` reports `adaptiveDetail.colCount`.": "",
  "The open detail directly after its row, with `rowType: 'detailAdaptive'`, before the row's master-detail.": ""
}
